    "Synthetic sessions are 50 paired loopback TCP conversations under one executable group; the real session, when measured, is named by the INTERCAT_REAL_SESSION variable and stays local.",
    "Each synthetic session is measured twice: derived from its segments, and then reopened from the derivation checkpoint and persisted overview its writer published (derivation-checkpoint-v1, overview-v1), which the second open reads instead of any segment."
